  "lineage": "Japanese screen and game scoring consolidated from the 1950s onward — Toru Takemitsu's sparse modernist film scores for Kobayashi and Teshigahara, Joe Hisaishi's minimalist ostinato-and-melody writing for Miyazaki from 1984, Ryuichi Sakamoto's synth-and-orchestra hybrids, and the game lineage of Koichi Sugiyama and Nobuo Uematsu whose chiptune themes were later rescored for full orchestra — built on long-breathed diatonic or yo-scale themes, ostinato piano or harp figuration, restrained rubato, and orchestral colour weighted toward strings, woodwind solos and celesta.",
